**consolidated/unknown/1790227857601** (memory): WebSocket protocol tunneling and byte forwarding should preserve transport abstraction boundaries—never modify the tunneled protocol itself, only wrap/unwrap the transport layer. The pattern appears in three contexts: (1) Hocuspocus bytes tunneling through plan-channel, (2) channel-websocket using WebSocketPolyfill with transportFor, (3) run-feed forwarding notifications. Agents should isolate transport concerns from business logic and avoid creating multiple listeners on the same socket unless each explicitly ignores foreign paths and never destroys shared resources.
